  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Add multiple LOCAL save slots, accessible from the root radial menu or quick actions, for the values of the expression parameters of the currently worn avatar that are marked in the SDK as \"saved\". One save slot would be selected at all times, defaulting to \"1\".\n\nChanging save slots would function exactly like loading an avatar with saved parameters already does, with the animator controllers running from their entry states with these parameters set. The only difference is that changing the parameters in one slot would not affect the saved parameters in the other slots.\n\nResetting an avatar would apply to the currently selected slot only. \n\nDeleting local data would clear all save slots. The objective of this feature is to streamline changes in avatar settings for complex avatars, not to guarantee long term persistence of the saved data.\n\nNon-saved parameters would be entirely unaffected (but since changing slots would restart the avatar, non-saved parameters should probably return to default values at this point).\n\nThe currently selected save slot should probably be stored separately for each avatar for which a save slot was explicitly selected (rather than the default).",
